agm: 1.0
package: api.exceptions
version: 0.1.0
title: API Exception Catalogue

node api.exception.rate_limit_exceeded
type: exception
summary: client has exceeded the allowed request rate and must back off before retrying
priority: high
stability: high
detail:
  This exception occurs when a client exceeds the rate limit for an endpoint.
  The server returns HTTP 429 Too Many Requests with the following headers:

    Retry-After: <seconds until the limit resets>
    X-RateLimit-Limit: <max requests per window>
    X-RateLimit-Remaining: 0
    X-RateLimit-Reset: <unix timestamp of window reset>

resolution:
  Client MUST wait for the duration specified in Retry-After before sending
  another request. Clients SHOULD implement exponential backoff with jitter
  to avoid thundering-herd effects when the window resets.
notes:
  Persistent violations (rate limit hit more than 5 times per hour) trigger
  an alert and may result in temporary IP or API key suspension.
